e name pattern, compiled case-insensitively, placed after `MAX_AGE_SECONDS`.\n- **`_purge_not_constructed(conn)`**: finds stored `Tournaments/Topdeck/%` events whose name matches, then in one transaction clears `duplicate_of` pointing at them and deletes their rows from `meta_deck_archetype`, `meta_round_match`, `meta_deck` and `meta_event`. It rolls back and re-raises on error and logs one warning with the count. It does nothing when nothing matches.\n- **`refresh_topdeck`**: skips a tournament whose name matches, with a warning and a count in `skipped`. It calls the purge right after `store_events`.\n\nI did not run the full test suite or the dashboard checks, since the spec only lists these two commands. The changes are uncommitted in the worktree.", "ttft_ms": 1931, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 20510, "uuid": "0230b70e-52e3-42a6-9d32-d469972856ba", "ttft_stream_ms": 1617, "time_to_request_ms": 592, "first_content_frame_ms": 1617, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}
